@base_url = http://localhost:8080/api/listings

### happy path: create a need
POST  {{base_url}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "categoryId": 1,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 10,
  "quantityRemaining": 10,
  "urgency": "HIGH",
  "neededBy": "2026-09-30",
  "status": "OPEN"
}

### Need2
POST  {{base_url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 2,
  "categoryId": 1,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 10,
  "quantityRemaining": 10,
  "urgency": "MEDIUM",
  "neededBy": "2026-09-30",
  "status": "OPEN"
}

### Happy path: Create a SURPLUS
POST {{base_url}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 2,
  "categoryId": 1,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 7,
  "quantityRemaining": 7,
  "availableUntil": "2026-10-10",
  "status": "OPEN"
}

### happy path: find by id
GET {{base_url}}/8 HTTP/1.1


### happy path: find by userId
GET {{base_url}}/myListings?userId=1


### happy path: update a listing
PUT {{base_url}}/12?requesterId=2 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 5,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 10,
  "quantityRemaining": 10,
  "availableUntil": "2026-10-19",
  "status": "OPEN"
}


### delete
DELETE {{base_url}}/22?requesterId=2

### findAll 
GET {{base_url}}



### ============================================================================
### ShareBoard seed data — IntelliJ HTTP Client format
### Run top to bottom, in order (later requests depend on earlier ones' IDs
### being captured into variables). Open this file in IntelliJ and click the
### green ▶ next to each request, or use "Run All Requests in File".
###
### Why .http instead of SQL for this part: these go through your REAL
### /api/auth/register endpoint (so passwords are actually hashed and you can
### really log in as these accounts) and your REAL matching engine (so every
### match that happens here creates a genuine, consistent match_line row —
### no risk of the "matched but no history" bug from directly-inserted data).
###
### You still need categories seeded first — there's no POST endpoint for
### those. Run this tiny SQL snippet once before this file:
###
###   USE shareboard;
###   INSERT INTO category (id, name) VALUES
###     (1, 'Blankets'), (2, 'Canned Food'), (3, 'Baby Formula'),
###     (4, 'Coats'), (5, 'School Supplies'), (6, 'Hygiene Kits');
###
### ============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Register accounts (orgs get the verified badge; a couple of individuals too)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register riverside_shelter
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "riverside_shelter",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("shelterId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register corner_market
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "corner_market",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("marketId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register hope_nursery
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "hope_nursery",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("nurseryId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register downtown_pharmacy
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "downtown_pharmacy",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("pharmacyId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register eastside_foodbank
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "eastside_foodbank",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("foodbankId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register community_pantry
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "community_pantry",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": true
}

> {%
    client.global.set("pantryId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register j_rivera (individual, not an org)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "j_rivera",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": false
}

> {%
    client.global.set("riveraId", response.body.userId);
%}

### Register m_chen (individual, not an org)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "m_chen",
  "passwordHash": "Password123!",
  "organization": false
}

> {%
    client.global.set("chenId", response.body.userId);
%}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Pair 1: Blankets — will auto-match FULLY the instant the surplus posts
### (posted anonymously, so it should show as "Anonymous Donor" everywhere)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NEED: Blankets, 50 units, riverside_shelter
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{shelterId}},
  "categoryId": 1,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 50,
  "quantityRemaining": 50,
  "urgency": "HIGH",
  "neededBy": "2026-10-20",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}

### SURPLUS: Blankets, 50 units, corner_market, anonymous — matches the need above
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{marketId}},
  "categoryId": 1,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 50,
  "quantityRemaining": 50,
  "availableUntil": "2026-11-01",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": true
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Pair 2: Baby Formula — surplus only partially covers the need (20 of 30),
### leaving the need PARTIALLY_MATCHED with 10 still open
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NEED: Baby Formula, 30 units, hope_nursery
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{nurseryId}},
  "categoryId": 3,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 30,
  "quantityRemaining": 30,
  "urgency": "MEDIUM",
  "neededBy": "2026-10-25",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}

### SURPLUS: Baby Formula, 20 units, downtown_pharmacy — partially fills the need above
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{pharmacyId}},
  "categoryId": 3,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 20,
  "quantityRemaining": 20,
  "availableUntil": "2026-10-30",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Pair 3: Baby Formula — deliberately incompatible dates, so the deadline-
### crossing check correctly REJECTS this match. Good one to point at live.
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NEED: Baby Formula, 15 units, needed by Nov 10 — far out deadline
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{nurseryId}},
  "categoryId": 3,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 15,
  "quantityRemaining": 15,
  "urgency": "LOW",
  "neededBy": "2026-11-10",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}

### SURPLUS: Baby Formula, 10 units, expires Oct 5 — BEFORE the need's deadline, won't match
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{pharmacyId}},
  "categoryId": 3,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 10,
  "quantityRemaining": 10,
  "availableUntil": "2026-10-05",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Pair 4: Coats — need fully covered, surplus has extra left over (partial
### match on the surplus side: need becomes MATCHED, surplus stays OPEN with
### 10 remaining)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NEED: Coats, 30 units, riverside_shelter
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{shelterId}},
  "categoryId": 4,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 30,
  "quantityRemaining": 30,
  "urgency": "LOW",
  "neededBy": "2026-11-15",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}

### SURPLUS: Coats, 40 units, corner_market — covers the need above with 10 left over
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{marketId}},
  "categoryId": 4,
  "type": "SURPLUS",
  "quantity": 40,
  "quantityRemaining": 40,
  "availableUntil": "2026-12-01",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Withdrawn example — post it, then withdraw it
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### NEED: School Supplies, 25 units — about to be withdrawn
POST {{baseUrl}}/listings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": {{shelterId}},
  "categoryId": 5,
  "type": "NEED",
  "quantity": 25,
  "quantityRemaining": 25,
  "urgency": "LOW",
  "neededBy": "2026-10-15",
  "status": "OPEN",
  "anonymous": false
}

> {%
    client.global.set("toWithdrawId", response.body.listingId);
%}

### Withdraw it (requesterId must match the owner — riverside_shelter)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/listings/{{toWithdrawId}}?requesterId={{shelterId}}


